# PalengkeGo configuration reference
#
# The app reads ALL configuration from compile-time dart-defines — there is no
# runtime .env loading. `.env` no longer exists; this file documents the keys.
#
# Build with backend enabled, e.g.:
#
#   flutter build apk --release \
#     --dart-define=APP_ENV=production \
#     --dart-define=FIREBASE_ENABLED=true \
#     --dart-define=SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co \
#     --dart-define=SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIs... \
#     --dart-define=PAYMONGO_PUBLIC_KEY=pk_test_xxx
#
# KEY ORIGIN
#   APP_ENV            development (default) | staging | production
#   FIREBASE_ENABLED   true only when lib/firebase_options.dart is present
#                      (run `flutterfire configure` — the file is gitignored)
#   SUPABASE_URL       Supabase dashboard > Settings > API > Project URL
#   SUPABASE_ANON_KEY  Supabase dashboard > Settings > API > anon/public key
#   PAYMONGO_PUBLIC_KEY  PayMongo dashboard (pk_test_xxx / pk_live_xxx)
#
# SECURITY
#   Only PUBLIC keys belong in dart-defines: Supabase anon key and PayMongo
#   public key are safe to ship. NEVER compile in:
#     - Supabase `service_role` key (full database access)
#     - PayMongo secret key (sk_test_ / sk_live_)
#   Payment intents/links must be created on the backend only.
#
# WITHOUT any dart-defines the app boots in demo/mock mode (local repositories).
